{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLqBLeD4YmTgdy6QqNgW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the LaTeX output for both cases from the issue, in `sympy/printing/latex.py`.\n\n- `(1/20)**(1/30)` now prints as `\\left(\\frac{1}{20}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{30}}`.\n- `(1/1)**(1/1)` now prints as `\\left(\\frac{1}{1}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{1}}`.\n- `(10/1)**(20/1)` and `2**(3/2)` print as before.\n\nBefore the fix, the unevaluated product `Mul(1, Pow(20, -1))` went through the branch that prints every factor literally, which gave `1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{20}`. I added an exception for a two-factor product of a number and the reciprocal of a number, so it prints as a fraction instead. Other unevaluated products still print literally.\n\n`sympy/printing/tests/test_latex.py` passes: 170 passed, 2 xfailed. I didn't add a test for the new output."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":750,"cache_read_input_tokens":23307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":750},"output_tokens":329,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62d09696-9bbf-42b3-bcd9-d61cebc6c56f","uuid":"6a51162b-84fa-4bc5-bc23-eb6abcc6e3f9","timestamp":"2026-11-24T00:47:28.393Z","request_id":"req_011ChLqBKgQL2KUgH5Ec2V3K"}
